I'm Robert Wilson I won the 1978 Nobel  Prize in Physics for discovering cosmic  microwave background radiation which is  radiation left over from the Big Bang I  went to Bell Labs in 1963 and one of the  things we wanted to do was to make a  measurement of the minimum brightness of  the sky and that went horribly wrong we  kept making measurements and kept seeing  the same extra radiation but we were  scratching our heads trying to  understand where it might come from well  we worried about a pair of pigeons that  are living in the antenna and they had  dropped pigeon droppings all over the  inside and what we did was to get a have  a heart trap pigeons went in trapped  closed  we took the pigeons put them in a box  mailed them as far as way as we could in  the company mail to a guy who fancied  pigeons and he looked at them and said  these are junk pigeons and let them go  and before long they were right back  we had ruled out a man-made radiation  and I don't remember what else but any  other imperfections we might have been  able to think of we were really running  out of ideas when we heard about the  idea of radiation left over from the Big  Bang  what you're hearing now is a recording  that I made  and several years later but in a  fraction like fifteen percent of this  noise comes from the cosmic microwave  background radiation our understanding  is that the universe was created from a  very compact way and it had been  expanded ever since  the beautiful bay above tree or Tree of  Life is an African icon the bail Bob  fruit contains four times the potassium  of banana three times the vitamin C of  an orange and twice the calcium of  spinach but the bail Bob is an orphan  science has paid little attention to  this tree until now the African orphan  crops consortium is harnessing the power  of genetics for orphan crops the bail  Bob tree is the first of 101 plants to  have its genome sequence assembled and  annotated and the information will be  made available to all unrestricted where  millions of people are malnourished this  genetic data will help farmers provide  the food they need the genomes will  guide African plant breeders so they can  create crops that are higher yielding  water and nutrient use sufficient  resilient to climate change and full of  nutrition triggering a huge leap forward  for the diversity and sustainability of  the continents agriculture
 

